WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.650
Where does Infoblox fit?

2
00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:06.094
Where the Grid already runs the
agency's DNS, vNIOS is the choice,

3
00:00:06.094 --> 00:00:11.050
because it joins the same Grid and
gets its policy from the Grid Master.

4
00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:13.512
The same criteria apply as for BIND.

5
00:00:13.512 --> 00:00:17.012
Confirm its failover in
GovCloud and Azure Government.

6
00:00:17.012 --> 00:00:18.980
The open points for this part:

7
00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:23.901
whether Oracle's VCN resolver passes
DNSSEC data to a resolver behind it,

8
00:00:23.901 --> 00:00:29.149
and whether CISA's Protective DNS
returns DNSSEC data to agency forwarders.

9
00:00:29.149 --> 00:00:33.225
And the illustrative configuration
hasn't yet run in a VPC.

10
00:00:33.225 --> 00:00:37.552
The next steps: ask the seven
questions of every cloud BIND server,

11
00:00:37.552 --> 00:00:42.199
build the forwarder pattern in a test
account in each Region and realm,

12
00:00:42.199 --> 00:00:45.725
and run Book 08's validation
matrix from every origin.

13
00:00:45.725 --> 00:00:50.650
This is research under review, not an
endorsement by any federal agency.

14
00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:51.480
Thank you.
